From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jake Cattrall <krazyjakee@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:13:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vello_hybrid: report a failed start instead of panicking, and
 optionally refuse software adapters

When no surface, adapter, device or surface renderer can be had, resume
leaves the renderer in a failed state (complete_resume returns false,
failure() says why) and still calls on_ready, instead of panicking. With
allow_software_adapter(false), starting on wgpu's DeviceType::Cpu (llvmpipe,
lavapipe, WARP) fails the same way, so an embedder can draw with a CPU
renderer that repaints only damage instead of rasterising in software
through a GPU API.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
